#3115
The Belfry of the Drowned Bell~
   The belfry is open to the weather on all four sides, and its bell
swings very slightly in the wind with a sound too low to be called
ringing.  From here the drowned cloister can be seen entire:  the
garth, the roofs, and the ash-coloured tower far off across the
flood.~
