#3119
The Tomb of Abbot Mael~
   The tomb is a round chamber under the east end of the hall, its
dome painted with a sea that has no shore.  A sarcophagus of green
stone stands at the centre, and the water about it is black and
unmoving.  A stair at the chamber's north side goes down into the
darkness beneath the cloister.~
