#3121
The Gate Beneath the Water~
   Two pillars of black basalt rise out of the flood here, and between
them a road of fitted stone runs north into a cutting in the rock.
The water runs off it in a thin ribbon and does not pool.  Above and
behind, the green water of the valley lies still;  ahead, a red
light moves somewhere under the ash-coloured stone.~
